 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, one after the other. Before attempts 2 through 5,
+larder waits 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds respectively. A successful attempt returns immediately; if all attempts time out,
+the final `GatewayTimeout` is raised. The pauses add up to 20 seconds of waiting on the confirmation page, in addition
+to the time spent calling the gateway.
+
+Previously, three attempts ran back to back within a second. During the gateway's Friday peak, 17:00 to 19:00,
+all three could hit the same slow period: 58 confirmed pantry orders went uncharged and a payments volunteer captured
+them by hand the next morning. A sandbox replay with the current retry schedule would have captured 57 of those 58
+pantry orders. The maintainers accepted the extra wait to reduce that manual work. Switching gateways was also
+considered, but the existing contract runs through December 2026. [Issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md) records the
+discussion and acceptance.
 
